This project, rememberfetch is a fetch tool written fully in C.

The goal of this project is to be as wildly efficient as possible,
and simple as possible.

This fetch tool will merely read the amount of ram in use/total and
your linux distro.

Supported operating systems include linux. (yes, thats it)

This fetch tool is written purely for fun and I have no intention of
maintaining it once I create it.

BUILDING AND INSTALLING
Currently the only way to install rememberfetch is to compile it manually
using GCC and make:

make: compiles and outputs binary to current directory

make install: compiles and installs program to /bin (must be run as root)

make clean: removes binary from current directory

make uninstall: removes binary from /bin (must be run as root)
